# G11-D (contract §3, PM ruling R-2026-09-17-3 R2/R3): the independent
# `mcs251-placement-verify` executable, exercised on a REAL B+C product.
#
# Every negative here starts from a set that VERIFIED, mutates exactly one
# carrier (final ELF / report / input object / manifest / link map), and then
# runs the VERIFIER directly -- never the linker, which would refuse the
# mutation first and hide the verifier's own detection power (contract §5).
# Each case asserts the exit code AND the target diagnostic, so a generic
# input rejection cannot pass for a detection.
#
# Capability is present in this tree, so a compile/link/parse/locate/verify
# failure is a FAIL, never a SKIP.  Only spec-defined non-applicabilities are
# exempt (NOBITS has no CODE bytes; a bind function's size is unchecked).
#
# G11-C2 (PM rulings R-2026-09-17-4 / R-2026-09-18-1): the linker now CONSUMES
# the `.mcs251.placement.names` association carrier the frozen emitter writes,
# so the carrier-backed bind positive and the V17 bind-relocation positive are
# reachable with a REAL B+C product (llc -> lld -> verifier) and are asserted
# below.  The pre-C2 "registered cross-slice blocker" is closed; only the
# deliberate legacy-object boundary (a bind object WITHOUT a carrier must be
# refused) remains, and it is driven by a synthetic carrier-less object so the
# real emitter can no longer produce it.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: llc -mtriple=mcs251 -O0 -filetype=obj -mcs251-object-format=elf p.ll -o p.o
# RUN: llc -mtriple=mcs251 -O0 -filetype=obj -mcs251-object-format=elf bind.ll -o bind.o

# =====================================================================
# rule V0 - the tool exists and is a real independent process.  A suite that "goes
# green" because the verifier is missing is exactly what the contract forbids,
# so this is a positive assertion, not a `not`.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: mcs251-placement-verify --version | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VER
# VER: mcs251-placement-verify
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --nonsense 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BADOPT
# BADOPT: unknown option --nonsense
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=p.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REQ
# REQ: --elf and --report are required

# =====================================================================
# V-positive: the real product verifies; --verify-placement drives it as a
# child process, success is silent, and the report+verify grid publishes one
# report byte stream.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: mcs251-lld p.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 --area-start=VECS=0xff0003 --area-start=BOOT=0xff0100 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0200 --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --area-start=XDATA_INIT=0xff9000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --placement-report=p.placement --verify-placement --map=p.map -o p.elf 2>v.err
# RUN: test ! -s v.err
# RUN: bash v.sh
# --- V1: an output without a symbol table fails closed with the frozen text,
# --- and the Driver adds no `mcs251-lld: error:` prefix to the verifier body.
# RUN: mcs251-lld p.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 --area-start=VECS=0xff0003 --area-start=BOOT=0xff0100 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0200 --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --area-start=XDATA_INIT=0xff9000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 -o nosym.elf
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --elf=nosym.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOSYM
# NOSYM: VERIFY FAIL: input ELF has no symbol table (relink with --verify-placement or --placement-report)
# NOSYM-NOT: mcs251-lld: error:

# =====================================================================
# C2-positive (a) - the REAL carrier-backed bind chain: llc emits a bind-only
# object whose `.mcs251.placement.names` carrier associates the record with the
# undefined external `_ghostx`; the linker consumes it (the stable name is
# `ghostx`, NOT the ELF name), publishes a bind-only report row, and the
# linker's own --verify-placement pass accepts it.  The row's ELF name is the
# ASSOCIATED name, proving the carrier -- not a stable==declaration-name
# assumption -- drove the mapping.  V17 then re-checks the bind relocation (a
# 24-bit address split over LO8/MID8/HI8 relocations) from the original object.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: mcs251-lld bind.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 --area-start=VECS=0xff0003 --area-start=BOOT=0xff0100 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0200 --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --area-start=XDATA_INIT=0xff9000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --placement-report=bind.placement --verify-placement --map=bind.map -o bind.elf 2>bind.err
# RUN: test ! -s bind.err
# RUN: FileCheck --input-file=bind.placement %s --check-prefix=BINDROW
# BINDROW: ghostx | _ghostx | {{.*}}bind.o |  | 0 | 0 | 1 | 0x00000080 | 4 | 1 | 0 | {{.*}} | 1
# RUN: mcs251-placement-verify --elf=bind.elf --report=bind.placement --object=bind.o --link-map=bind.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff
# --- V17 negative on the SAME real object: only the final relocated byte
# --- (LO8 of the 24-bit address) changes, so the encoding must be re-derived.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-poke bind.elf mut.elf 0xff0202 000081
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=mut.elf --report=bind.placement --object=bind.o --link-map=bind.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V17BC
# V17BC: VERIFY FAIL: relocation to ghostx at 0x{{[0-9a-f]+}} does not encode the expected placement address

# =====================================================================
# rule V2 - original NOTE structure.  Each mutation is a pure byte edit of p.o, so
# the only difference from the verified set is the damaged record table.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py note-namesz p.o mut.o 0x8
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env OBJ=mut.o bash v.sh 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V2N
# V2N: VERIFY FAIL: malformed placement NOTE in mut.o: namesz 8 != 7
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py note-pad p.o mut.o dv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env OBJ=mut.o bash v.sh 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V2P
# V2P: VERIFY FAIL: malformed placement NOTE in mut.o: record {{[0-9]+}} at offset {{[0-9]+}}: non-zero padding
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py note-truncate p.o mut.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env OBJ=mut.o bash v.sh 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V2T
# V2T: VERIFY FAIL: malformed placement NOTE in mut.o: record {{[0-9]+}} at offset {{[0-9]+}}: record_size does not fit the remaining NOTE data

# =====================================================================
# rule V3 - a LEGACY bind object (bind record, no association carrier) must be
# refused outright -- the stable is never used to guess the ELF name.  The C2
# emitter always writes the carrier, so this deliberate boundary is driven by a
# synthetic carrier-less object (bind-id-nocarrier.yaml) rather than the real
# llc product; the verifier's V3 path is shared with the linker's own rule.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: yaml2obj bind-id-nocarrier.yaml -o bind-legacy-v1.o && %python seteflags.py bind-legacy-v1.o && mv bind-legacy-v1.o bind-legacy.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env OBJ=bind-legacy.o bash v.sh 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V3B
# V3B: VERIFY FAIL: missing placement name association for {{.*}} in bind-legacy.o (recompile placement object)

# =====================================================================
# rule V4 - each original record's own H_source, recomputed from its own fields.
# The corrupted record keeps its neighbour rows intact, so only V4 can fire.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py note-flip-hash p.o mut.o cl
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env OBJ=mut.o bash v.sh 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V4
# V4: VERIFY FAIL: layout hash mismatch for cl: record {{[0-9]+}} in mut.o stores {{.*}} but its own recorded fields hash to

# =====================================================================
# rule V5 - the manifest is re-read and its explicit values are checked; the SAME
# path the link consumed is edited, so the failure is the field mismatch and
# not a "source path appeared/disappeared" artifact.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: printf 'place ghost 0x10000 xdata size=4 bind\n' > m.txt
# RUN: mcs251-lld p.o --placement-manifest=m.txt --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 --area-start=VECS=0xff0003 --area-start=BOOT=0xff0100 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0200 --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --area-start=XDATA_INIT=0xff9000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --placement-report=m.placement --verify-placement --map=m.map -o m.elf
# RUN: env ELF=m.elf REPORT=m.placement MAP=m.map bash v.sh --placement-manifest=m.txt
# RUN: printf 'place ghost 0x10000 xdata size=8 bind\n' > m.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env ELF=m.elf REPORT=m.placement MAP=m.map bash v.sh --placement-manifest=m.txt 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V5S
# V5S: VERIFY FAIL: placement report field size mismatch for ghost
# RUN: printf 'place ghost 0x10000 xdata size=4 bind noinit\n' > m.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env ELF=m.elf REPORT=m.placement MAP=m.map bash v.sh --placement-manifest=m.txt 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V5B
# V5B: VERIFY FAIL: malformed placement manifest entry for ghost
# RUN: printf 'place ghost 0x10000 xdata size=4 bind\n' > m.txt

# =====================================================================
# rule V6 - the independent semantic merge and its precedence.  Every mutation is
# applied to ALL carriers consistently so the failure lands on the merge rule,
# never on an incidental hash or span disagreement.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --object=p.o --object=p.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V6D
# V6D: VERIFY FAIL: placement NOTE duplicate owned record for cl in p.o and
# --- two non-1 align values that disagree: the owned NOTE says 2, a manifest
# --- row says 4.  The NOTE hash and the report row are updated together.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-field p.placement mut.placement dv align 2
# RUN: printf 'place dv 0x40 data size=4 align=4\n' > a.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env MUT=%S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py bash vm.sh note-align dv 0x2 -- --report=mut.placement --placement-manifest=a.txt 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V6A
# V6A: VERIFY FAIL: conflicting placement for dv: manifest align disagrees ({{.*}}a.txt:1)
# --- a non-bind policy marker cannot manufacture a policy the owned NOTE
# --- does not carry.
# RUN: printf 'place dv 0x40 data size=4 retain\n' > r.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --placement-manifest=r.txt 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V6R
# V6R: VERIFY FAIL: conflicting placement for dv: manifest [retain] contradicts the owned NOTE ({{.*}}r.txt:1)

# =====================================================================
# rule V7 - strict report syntax and explicit field cross-check.  The layout_hash is
# RECOMPUTED for the edited row, so a hash failure cannot be mistaken for the
# field check and the report cannot act as its own oracle.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-field p.placement mut.placement dv class 1
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V7C
# V7C: VERIFY FAIL: placement report field class mismatch for dv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-field p.placement mut.placement dv entity 1
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V7E
# V7E: VERIFY FAIL: placement report field entity mismatch for dv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-field p.placement mut.placement dv ownership 1
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V7O
# V7O: VERIFY FAIL: placement report field ownership mismatch for dv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-field p.placement mut.placement dv align 2
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V7A
# V7A: VERIFY FAIL: placement report field align mismatch for dv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-field p.placement mut.placement dv flags 2
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V7F
# V7F: VERIFY FAIL: placement report field flags mismatch for dv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-field p.placement mut.placement dv size 8
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V7S
# V7S: VERIFY FAIL: placement report field size mismatch for dv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-field p.placement mut.placement dv bound_only 1
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V7B
# V7B: VERIFY FAIL: placement report field bound_only mismatch for dv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-reverse p.placement mut.placement
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V7R
# V7R: VERIFY FAIL: malformed placement report at line 2: rows are not in (stable, file, sym, section) byte order

# =====================================================================
# rule V8 - bidirectional enumeration, driven by the original records and manifest
# rows -- never by the report.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-drop p.placement mut.placement nv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V8M
# V8M: VERIFY FAIL: no placement report row for placement record nv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-add p.placement mut.placement p
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V8E
# V8E: VERIFY FAIL: placement report row _zz has no NOTE/manifest source

# =====================================================================
# rule V9 - the report's own H_report.  Flipping one bit of the stored value must
# fail even though every explicit field is intact.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-flip-hash p.placement mut.placement dv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V9
# V9: VERIFY FAIL: layout hash mismatch for _dv: report line {{[0-9]+}} stores

# =====================================================================
# rule V10 - the output entity, its address and the synthetic bind-only shape.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-stvalue p.elf mut.elf _dv 0x44
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --elf=mut.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V10A
# V10A: VERIFY FAIL dv: address 0x44 != expected 0x40
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-rename p.elf mut.elf _xv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --elf=mut.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V10E
# V10E: VERIFY FAIL: no output entity for placement record xv

# =====================================================================
# rule V11 - sizes and main-symbol shape.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-size p.elf mut.elf _xv 0x8
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --elf=mut.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V11
# V11: VERIFY FAIL xv: size 8 != recorded 4

# =====================================================================
# rule V12 - the merged alignment is executed, and the class's address space holds.
# The NOTE address, its record hash, the report row and the output st_value
# are all moved together, so the verdict can only come from the range rules.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-field p.placement mut.placement entryf address 0xfc4001
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-stvalue p.elf mut.elf _entryf 0xfc4001
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py map-section p.map mut2.map p.o:.mcu.fixed.entryf 0xfc4001
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env MUT=%S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py bash vm.sh note-addr entryf 0xfc4001 -- --report=mut.placement --elf=mut.elf --link-map=mut2.map 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V12A
# V12A: VERIFY FAIL: entryf at 0xfc4001 violates alignment 4
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-field p.placement mut2.placement dv address 0xffff
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-stvalue p.elf mut2.elf _dv 0xffff
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py map-section p.map v12b.map p.o:.mcu.fixed.dv 0xffff
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env MUT=%S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py bash vm.sh note-addr dv 0xffff -- --report=mut2.placement --elf=mut2.elf --link-map=v12b.map 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V12B
# V12B: VERIFY FAIL: dv [0xffff,0x10003) outside AS0-DATA address space

# =====================================================================
# rule V13 - the window is the INDEPENDENT board-level number, never the map's
# "already placed here".  Nothing but the window changes here.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=p.elf --report=p.placement --object=p.o --link-map=p.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x3000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V13
# V13: VERIFY FAIL: entryf [0xfc4000,0xfc4001) outside CODE window
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=p.elf --report=p.placement --object=p.o --link-map=p.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --xdata-size=0x1000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V13X
# V13X: VERIFY FAIL: xv [0x20000,0x20004) outside XDATA capacity window

# =====================================================================
# rule V14 - overlap accounting counts each entity once per storage space.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-field p.placement mut.placement nv address 0x40
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-stvalue p.elf mut.elf _nv 0x40
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py map-section p.map v14.map p.o:.mcu.fixed.nv 0x40
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env MUT=%S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py bash vm.sh note-addr nv 0x40 -- --report=mut.placement --elf=mut.elf --link-map=v14.map 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V14
# V14: VERIFY FAIL: dv overlaps nv

# =====================================================================
# rule V15 - retain, in both directions, and the report marker.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env MUT=%S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py bash vm.sh sec-flags .mcu.fixed.rv 0x3 -- 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V15A
# V15A: VERIFY FAIL: retain flag mismatch for rv in p.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 env MUT=%S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py bash vm.sh sec-flags .text 0x200006 -- 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V15B
# V15B: VERIFY FAIL: retain flag mismatch for .text in p.o: SHF_GNU_RETAIN outside .mcu.fixed.*
# --- the frozen V15 diagnostic must stay reachable even when an earlier check
# --- has its own verdict for the same artifact (it used to be swallowed by
# --- V8's missing-row return).
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-drop p.placement mut.placement rv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V15C
# V15C: VERIFY FAIL: retained entity rv absent from placement report/symtab
# V15C: VERIFY FAIL: no placement report row for placement record rv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-rename p.elf mut.elf _rv _gone
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --elf=mut.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V15D
# V15D: VERIFY FAIL: retained entity rv absent from placement report/symtab

# =====================================================================
# rule V16 - noinit initialization coverage.  The table location comes from the
# FINAL ELF's s_/l_ symbols, cross-checked against the map's boundary rows; a
# missing, zeroed or malformed boundary row is a FAIL (contract section 4 / R3),
# never "this image has no audited initialization path".
# =====================================================================
# --- locating evidence that DISAGREES with the final ELF: a shortened table
# --- (old behavior: rc=0, the whole noinit check silently dropped).
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py map-bound p.map mut.map l_XINIT 0x0
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --link-map=mut.map 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V16B
# V16B: VERIFY FAIL: malformed link map mut.map: the XINIT boundary disagrees with the final ELF
# --- a boundary row that is not even a number is malformed evidence, not a row
# --- to drop.
# RUN: sed 's/^l_XINIT = .*/l_XINIT = garbage/' p.map > mut.map
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --link-map=mut.map 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V16M
# V16M: VERIFY FAIL: malformed link map mut.map: bad boundary value in l_XINIT = garbage
# --- an initialization record whose destination was moved onto the noinit
# --- entity: the record is decoded from the FINAL image.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-poke p.elf mut.elf 0xff8000 0060
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --elf=mut.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V16C
# V16C: VERIFY FAIL: noinit entity nv is covered by XINIT initialization
# --- a truncated final table is malformed evidence.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-poke p.elf mut.elf 0xff8002 0000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --elf=mut.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V16R
# V16R: VERIFY FAIL: malformed XINIT initialization record at 0xff8000: bad object/payload length
# --- R2-5 (B4): a boundary key that appears TWICE with CONFLICTING values
# --- does not uniquely locate the table; the first match must not silently
# --- decide where the initialization tables live.  Pre-fix behavior: rc=0.
# RUN: cp p.map mut.map && echo 'l_XINIT = 0x0000' >> mut.map
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --link-map=mut.map 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=R25
# R25: VERIFY FAIL: malformed link map mut.map: the boundary row l_XINIT appears with conflicting values

# =====================================================================
# rule V18 - every owned CODE span byte must exist in the final load image, and a
# non-relocated byte must equal the input byte.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-codebyte p.elf mut.elf 0xfc0000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --elf=mut.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V18
# V18: VERIFY FAIL: CODE image mismatch for cl at 0xfc0000

# =====================================================================
# rule V17 - bind-only relocation encoding.  The positive uses a manifest-only
# bind entity (`ghost`, an XDATA object) referenced by an R_MCS251_24 in `.text`;
# the real carrier-backed bind positive lives in C2-positive (a) above, so this
# manifest-only channel additionally covers the grammar without a NOTE carrier.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: yaml2obj pointer.yaml -o pnt-v1.o && %python seteflags.py pnt-v1.o && mv pnt-v1.o pnt.o
# RUN: mcs251-lld pnt.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 --area-start=VECS=0xff0003 --area-start=BOOT=0xff0100 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0200 --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --area-start=XDATA_INIT=0xff9000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --placement-manifest=pnt.txt --placement-report=pnt.placement --verify-placement --map=pnt.map -o pnt.elf
# RUN: mcs251-placement-verify --elf=pnt.elf --report=pnt.placement --object=pnt.o --placement-manifest=pnt.txt --link-map=pnt.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff
# --- only the final relocated BYTES change: the encoding must be re-derived.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-codebyte pnt.elf mut.elf 0xff0200
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=mut.elf --report=pnt.placement --object=pnt.o --placement-manifest=pnt.txt --link-map=pnt.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V17B
# V17B: VERIFY FAIL: relocation to ghost at 0xff0200 does not encode the expected placement address
# --- an UNKNOWN relocation type must FAIL, never skip (it used to be able to
# --- mask a tampered final byte).  The object is mutated IN PLACE: its path is
# --- part of the map's locating evidence.
# RUN: cp pnt.o .pnt.pristine
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py rela-type pnt.o pnt.o .text 0 0xff
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py carrier-digest mut.elf mut.elf 0 pnt.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=mut.elf --report=pnt.placement --object=pnt.o --placement-manifest=pnt.txt --link-map=pnt.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V17U
# V17U: VERIFY FAIL: unknown relocation type 255 for ghost at 0xff0200 in pnt.o
# --- a relocation site outside the relocated input section is malformed.
# RUN: cp .pnt.pristine pnt.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py rela-offset pnt.o pnt.o .text 0 0x100
# RUN: cp pnt.elf v17s.elf
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py carrier-digest pnt.elf v17s.elf 0 pnt.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=v17s.elf --report=pnt.placement --object=pnt.o --placement-manifest=pnt.txt --link-map=pnt.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V17S
# V17S: VERIFY FAIL: relocation to ghost at {{.*}} lies outside the relocated input section .text in pnt.o
# RUN: cp .pnt.pristine pnt.o
# --- B10/R2: BOTH 16-bit channels are executable negatives from the
# --- verified R24 mother (the final encoding follows the channel width).
# --- The R_16 case predates the round; R_J16 is the registered
# --- old-0 -> new-1 pair of the first fix round.  Never source-only.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py rela-type pnt.o pnt.o .text 0 0x1
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-poke pnt.elf mut.elf 0xff0200 0000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py carrier-digest mut.elf mut.elf 0 pnt.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=mut.elf --report=pnt.placement --object=pnt.o --placement-manifest=pnt.txt --link-map=pnt.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V17C16
# V17C16: VERIFY FAIL: XDATA symbol ghost uses a 16-bit relocation channel
# RUN: cp .pnt.pristine pnt.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py rela-type pnt.o pnt.o .text 0 0x7
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-poke pnt.elf mut.elf 0xff0200 0000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py carrier-digest mut.elf mut.elf 0 pnt.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=mut.elf --report=pnt.placement --object=pnt.o --placement-manifest=pnt.txt --link-map=pnt.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V17CJ16
# V17CJ16: VERIFY FAIL: XDATA symbol ghost uses a 16-bit relocation channel
# RUN: cp .pnt.pristine pnt.o
# --- B10/R2: the stored-pointer span rule, as an executable isolation
# --- negative from the same mother: addend 5 (one past a size-4 object's
# --- one-past-end) with the final encoding moved to the byte-correct
# --- `01 00 05`.  Never source-only.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py rela-addend pnt.o pnt.o .text 0 0x5
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-poke pnt.elf mut.elf 0xff0200 010005
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py carrier-digest mut.elf mut.elf 0 pnt.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=mut.elf --report=pnt.placement --object=pnt.o --placement-manifest=pnt.txt --link-map=pnt.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V17P5
# V17P5: VERIFY FAIL: stored XDATA pointer resolves outside target object ghost
# RUN: cp .pnt.pristine pnt.o

# =====================================================================
# rule V18-reloc / V17 - an owned CODE object carrying a relocation.  The
# unknown type must not be able to mask the byte it nominally rewrites.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: yaml2obj code-reloc.yaml -o cr-v1.o && %python seteflags.py cr-v1.o && mv cr-v1.o code-reloc.o
# RUN: mcs251-lld code-reloc.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 --area-start=VECS=0xff0003 --area-start=BOOT=0xff0100 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0200 --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --area-start=XDATA_INIT=0xff9000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --placement-manifest=pnt.txt --placement-report=cr.placement --verify-placement --map=cr.map -o cr.elf
# RUN: cp code-reloc.o .cr.pristine
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py rela-type code-reloc.o code-reloc.o .mcu.fixed.fn 0 0xff
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-codebyte cr.elf mut.elf 0xfc1000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py carrier-digest mut.elf mut.elf 0 code-reloc.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=mut.elf --report=cr.placement --object=code-reloc.o --placement-manifest=pnt.txt --link-map=cr.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V18U
# V18U: VERIFY FAIL: unknown relocation type 255 for ghost at 0xfc1000 in code-reloc.o
# RUN: cp .cr.pristine code-reloc.o
# --- R2-4 (B5/V18): a J16 field encodes only the low 16 bits, so correct
# --- low bytes are not proof: the TARGET must live in the field's own 64K
# --- bank.  The owned CODE source sits at 0xfc1000, the CODE target at
# --- 0xff0200 -- cross-bank with a byte-correct low half.  Pre-fix
# --- behavior: rc=0 (old AND R1-fixed verifier both accepted it).
# RUN: yaml2obj j16.yaml -o j16-v1.o && %python seteflags.py j16-v1.o && mv j16-v1.o j16.o
# RUN: mcs251-lld j16.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 --area-start=VECS=0xff0003 --area-start=BOOT=0xff0100 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0200 --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --area-start=XDATA_INIT=0xff9000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --placement-report=j16.placement --verify-placement --map=j16.map -o j16.elf
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py rela-type j16.o j16.o .mcu.fixed.fn 0 0x7
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-poke j16.elf mut.elf 0xfc1000 0200
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py carrier-digest mut.elf mut.elf 0 j16.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=mut.elf --report=j16.placement --object=j16.o --link-map=j16.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=R24
# R24: VERIFY FAIL: CODE image mismatch for fn at 0xfc1000: the J16 target leaves the field's bank
# --- R3-3 (B5/V18 residue): the SAME-BANK J16 to a NON-bind XDATA target.
# The bank condition alone says nothing about the target's STORAGE SPACE:
# the producer's F9 gate refuses this input ("XDATA symbol ghost truncated
# to 16 bits"), so V18 must resolve the target's space independently and
# apply the same channel rule.  `ghost` here lives in a dynamically
# allocated `.mcs251.XSEG` at 0xfc0200 (same bank as fn at 0xfc1000); the
# R24 mother links fine, the channel is rewritten to J16 and the final
# encoding to the byte-correct `02 00` (third byte = input original).
# Pre-fix behavior: rc=0 (verifier) while the linker refuses.
# RUN: yaml2obj xdata-j16.yaml -o xj-v1.o && %python seteflags.py xj-v1.o && mv xj-v1.o xj.o
# RUN: mcs251-lld xj.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 --area-start=VECS=0xff0003 --area-start=BOOT=0xff0100 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0200 --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --area-start=XDATA_INIT=0xff9000 --area-start=XSEG=0xfc0200 --edata-end=0x3fff --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --placement-report=xj.placement --verify-placement --map=xj.map -o xj.elf
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py rela-type xj.o xj.o .mcu.fixed.fn 0 0x7
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-poke xj.elf mut.elf 0xfc1000 020000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py carrier-digest mut.elf mut.elf 0 xj.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=mut.elf --report=xj.placement --object=xj.o --link-map=xj.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0xfc0200 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=R33
# R33: VERIFY FAIL: CODE image mismatch for fn at 0xfc1000: the relocation targets XDATA symbol ghost through a 16-bit channel
# --- the retained positive: a same-bank J16 to a real CODE target links
# --- and verifies (the channel rule fires on the SPACE, never on the bank).
# RUN: yaml2obj samej16.yaml -o sj-v1.o && %python seteflags.py sj-v1.o && mv sj-v1.o samej16.o
# RUN: mcs251-lld samej16.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 --area-start=VECS=0xff0003 --area-start=BOOT=0xff0100 --area-start=CSEG=0xfc0200 --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --area-start=XDATA_INIT=0xff9000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --placement-report=sj.placement --verify-placement --map=sj.map -o sj.elf
# RUN: mcs251-placement-verify --elf=sj.elf --report=sj.placement --object=samej16.o --link-map=sj.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=CSEG=0xfc0200 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff

# =====================================================================
# rule B7 - the ELF/entity structure itself is evidence: a program header table
# that cannot be read, a misaligned NOTE carrier, or an owned output symbol that
# is no longer defined are all FAILs.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-phnum p.elf mut.elf 0xffff
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --elf=mut.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=B7P
# B7P: VERIFY FAIL: malformed input ELF mut.elf: program header table out of bounds
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py sec-align p.o mut.o .mcs251.placement 1
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --object=mut.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=B7A
# B7A: VERIFY FAIL: malformed placement NOTE in mut.o: carrier is not a flags=0 align=4 SHT_NOTE
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-undefined p.elf mut.elf _dv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --elf=mut.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=B7U
# B7U: VERIFY FAIL: invalid output symbol for placement record dv: not defined
# --- the frozen address/size wording: `VERIFY FAIL %sym: ...`, no colon after FAIL.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-stvalue p.elf mut.elf _dv 0x44
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --elf=mut.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FZA
# FZA: VERIFY FAIL dv: address 0x44 != expected 0x40
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-size p.elf mut.elf _dv 0x8
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --elf=mut.elf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FZS
# FZS: VERIFY FAIL dv: size 8 != recorded 4

# =====================================================================
# rule B2 - report strict parsing.  The overflow cases leave the stored hash
# untouched on purpose: the failure must come from the RANGE check, not from a
# stale hash.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-raw p.placement mut.placement dv size 4294967300
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=B2S
# B2S: VERIFY FAIL: malformed placement report at line {{[0-9]+}}: bad size column
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-raw p.placement mut.placement dv class 4294967296
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=B2C
# B2C: VERIFY FAIL: malformed placement report at line {{[0-9]+}}: bad class column
# --- the section column is cross-checked against the independently rebuilt
# --- source section, not accepted at face value.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-raw p.placement mut.placement dv section .wrong
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=B2X
# B2X: VERIFY FAIL: placement report field section mismatch for dv
# --- a second row for the same (file, sym, stable) triple is a duplicate even
# --- when its section column differs, and even when its hash is recomputed.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-dup p.placement mut.placement dv section .wrong
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=B2D
# B2D: VERIFY FAIL: duplicate placement report row for _dv
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-dup p.placement mut.placement dv class 1
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 bash v.sh --report=mut.placement 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=B2E
# B2E: VERIFY FAIL: duplicate placement report row for _dv

# =====================================================================
# rule B3 - V14 counts fixed x DYNAMIC storage too.  The link is a real product
# (p.o + a dynamic XSEG slice object); the fixed XDATA entity `xv` is then moved
# CONSISTENTLY (NOTE + record hash + report + output st_value + map row) onto
# the dynamic slice's bytes, which must overlap it.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: yaml2obj dynamic.yaml -o dyn-v1.o && %python seteflags.py dyn-v1.o && mv dyn-v1.o dyn.o
# RUN: mcs251-lld p.o dyn.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 --area-start=VECS=0xff0003 --area-start=BOOT=0xff0100 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0200 --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --area-start=XDATA_INIT=0xff9000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --placement-report=dyn.placement --verify-placement --map=dyn.map -o dyn.elf
# RUN: mcs251-placement-verify --elf=dyn.elf --report=dyn.placement --object=p.o --object=dyn.o --link-map=dyn.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff
# RUN: cp p.o .p.o.pristine
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py note-addr p.o p.o xv 0x10000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py report-field dyn.placement mut.placement xv address 0x10000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-stvalue dyn.elf mut.elf _xv 0x10000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py map-section dyn.map mut.map p.o:.mcu.fixed.xv 0x10000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py carrier-addr mut.elf mut.elf 0 p.o .mcu.fixed.xv 0x10000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=mut.elf --report=mut.placement --object=p.o --object=dyn.o --link-map=mut.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=B3
# B3: VERIFY FAIL: xv overlaps .mcs251.XSEG
# RUN: cp .p.o.pristine p.o

# =====================================================================
# rule R2-1 (B3) - the map row is only a CANDIDATE for a dynamic section's
# position; the FINAL ELF's own symbol table must confirm it.  Moving ONLY
# the map's dynamic XSEG row (the ELF keeps `dyn` at 0x10000) used to pass:
# the ledger then believed the slice lived at 0x30000 and every overlap
# against it was invisible.  Pre-fix behavior: rc=0.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py map-section dyn.map mut.map dyn.o:.mcs251.XSEG 0x30000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=dyn.elf --report=dyn.placement --object=p.o --object=dyn.o --link-map=mut.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=R21
# R21: VERIFY FAIL: malformed link map mut.map: the section .mcs251.XSEG of dyn.o is placed at 0x30000 but the positioning carrier places it at 0x10000

# =====================================================================
# rule R3-1 (R2-1 residue) - the named-symbol cross-check is only ADDITIONAL
# evidence.  A dynamic section with NO named FUNC/OBJECT symbol (anonymous,
# NOTYPE-only, or with the final symbol's name gone) used to leave its map
# row as the ONLY position evidence: moving the row moved the ledger.  The
# final ELF keeps no input section names, so the independent anchor is the
# REGION: the final ELF's s_XSEG/l_XSEG boundary symbols cross-checked
# against the map's own boundary rows, plus the CLI windows.  Pre-fix
# behavior for all three: rc=0.
# =====================================================================
# RUN: sed '/^Symbols:/,$d' dynamic.yaml > anon-nosyms.yaml
# RUN: printf 'Symbols:\n  - Name: textonly\n    Binding: STB_GLOBAL\n    Type: STT_OBJECT\n    Section: .text\n    Size: 3\n' >> anon-nosyms.yaml
# RUN: mv anon-nosyms.yaml anon.yaml
# RUN: yaml2obj anon.yaml -o anon-v1.o && %python seteflags.py anon-v1.o && mv anon-v1.o anon.o
# RUN: mcs251-lld p.o anon.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 --area-start=VECS=0xff0003 --area-start=BOOT=0xff0100 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0200 --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --area-start=XDATA_INIT=0xff9000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --placement-report=anon.placement --verify-placement --map=anon.map -o anon.elf
# RUN: sed 's/STT_OBJECT/STT_NOTYPE/' dynamic.yaml > notype.yaml
# RUN: yaml2obj notype.yaml -o notype-v1.o && %python seteflags.py notype-v1.o && mv notype-v1.o notype.o
# RUN: mcs251-lld p.o notype.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 --area-start=VECS=0xff0003 --area-start=BOOT=0xff0100 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0200 --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --area-start=XDATA_INIT=0xff9000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --placement-report=notype.placement --verify-placement --map=notype.map -o notype.elf
# --- anonymous and NOTYPE-only slices move their map row OUT of the region
# --- the final ELF's own boundary symbols describe.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py map-section anon.map mut.map anon.o:.mcs251.XSEG 0x30000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=anon.elf --report=anon.placement --object=p.o --object=anon.o --link-map=mut.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=R31A
# R31A: VERIFY FAIL: malformed link map mut.map: the section .mcs251.XSEG of anon.o is placed at 0x30000 but the positioning carrier places it at 0x10000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py map-section notype.map mut.map notype.o:.mcs251.XSEG 0x30000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=notype.elf --report=notype.placement --object=p.o --object=notype.o --link-map=mut.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=R31N
# R31N: VERIFY FAIL: malformed link map mut.map: the section .mcs251.XSEG of notype.o is placed at 0x30000 but the positioning carrier places it at 0x10000
# --- the input still owns a named OBJECT, but the FINAL symbol's name is
# --- gone (elf-rename keeps value/size/shndx): the row must not become
# --- map-decided again.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py elf-rename dyn.elf mut.elf dyn
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/audit-mutate.py map-section dyn.map mut.map dyn.o:.mcs251.XSEG 0x30000
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/expect-rc.py 1 mcs251-placement-verify --elf=mut.elf --report=dyn.placement --object=p.o --object=dyn.o --link-map=mut.map --flash-base=0xfc0000 --flash-size=0x40000 --area-start=XSEG=0x010000 --edata-end=0x3fff 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=R31D
# R31D: VERIFY FAIL: malformed link map mut.map: the section .mcs251.XSEG of dyn.o is placed at 0x30000 but the positioning carrier places it at 0x10000

# =====================================================================
# rule R3-2 (R2-2 residue) - the section-name vocabulary's MATCHING
# BOUNDARIES are frozen with classifySection: `.mcs251.dseg` only as the
# exact name (the prefixed family is `.mcs251.DSEG.`), likewise
# edata/EDATA., xinit/xinit., xdata_init/xdata_init., HOME/HOME., VECS/VECS.,
# BOOT/BOOT.; no lowercase iseg/sseg; no `.mcs251.BITINIT` ALLOC section.
# The producer refuses all ten spellings below ("unsupported ALLOC
# section"); the verifier must refuse the fabricated map row too, not
# trust it.  Pre-fix behavior: rc=0 for every one.
# =====================================================================
